<title>INDONESIA: Pirelli to supply cables to Indonesia.</title>
<headline>Pirelli to supply cables to Indonesia.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A unit of Italian tyre and cable maker Pirelli SpA signed a contract on Tuesday to supply fibre optic cables to PT Telekomunikasi Indonesia (Telkom) for the next three years.</p>
<p>&quot;This contract is the first commitment of Pirelli towards the Indonesian community,&quot; Roberto Porro, president director of PT Pirelli Cables Indonesia, said in a statement.</p>
<p>The statement did not mention the value of the contract.</p>
<p>The cables will be manufactured at Pirelli's new $50 million factory in Cikampek, West Java, which is expected to employ around 300 skilled workers, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
